    {
      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research a low-overhead comparison-sort replacement for the recursive randomized Lomuto quicksort. Start with deterministic median-of-three pivots, efficient two-sided partitioning, insertion sorting for small ranges, bounded recursion and a worst-case fallback; investigate duplicate-aware partitioning where useful. Removing pivot RNG calls is safe after generation and avoids races on the global RNG state. Compare the improved serial kernel with coarse-grained parallel sorting of disjoint partitions, using at most four workers and only threading facilities supported by the unchanged build. Tune general size/task cutoffs rather than specializing to benchmark inputs. Measure whole-program performance: at roughly 69 ms baseline runtime, task startup and synchronization could outweigh parallel gains.\",\"B\":\"Research integer radix sorting as an independent alternative to comparison sorting. Compare a simple buffered byte-wise LSD implementation against a wider-digit variant, balancing pass count, histogram footprint and memory traffic. Preserve signed int ordering: for 32-bit ints, sorting keys formed by XOR with the sign bit avoids assuming the generator always produces nonnegative values. Explore four-worker passes with private histograms, prefix-derived disjoint output ranges and stable scatter, without per-element atomics. Retain a serial path for small arrays. Use checked allocation sizes and a correct low-memory fallback. Ensure MD5 receives the actual final sorted buffer without an unnecessary final copy where possible. Select variants by end-to-end measurements, not pass count alone.\",\"C\":\"Research exact case-generation and other non-sorting overhead reductions, producing changes independently composable with A or B. The two multiply-with-carry RNG streams have serial dependencies; investigate modest unrolling first, then exact modular skip-ahead for independent contiguous generation chunks if justified. Chunk initialization must reproduce the original sequence, never use independent seeds. Preserve the fixed reference's unsigned arithmetic, conversion behavior and generated int bytes. In particular, do not replace drand(0, INT_MAX) with a raw RNG integer without proving equivalence: floating-point multiplication, division and truncation can affect results. Treat abs/INT_MIN behavior as another compatibility hazard. Consider generation/histogram fusion only as a separately measured integration. Preserve sortedness validation and MD5's sequential chaining; never substitute independent chunk digests or cached answers.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only programs and improvements delivered by the research trees. Keep the best validated standalone candidate and the baseline available. Treat A and B primarily as competing sorting engines; test C with each promising engine separately before considering more complex hybrids. Reconcile RNG ownership, worker scheduling, scratch buffers and final-buffer ownership explicitly. Require unchanged correctness checks plus source-level reasoning about edge cases, allocation handling and exact generated bytes. Preserve input/error behavior, sortedness checking, conditional MD5 computation and output formatting. Use the existing measurement protocol and fixed compiler, target and budgets. Compare complete programs, including generation, allocation and hashing; reject regressions and do not assume gains combine additively.\",\"analysis\":\"This run targets Problem B in src/quicksort.c, not the other supplied problems. The valid baseline averaged 0.06909 seconds over three tightly clustered samples and passed four correctness cases. No input sizes or phase timings are supplied, so bottleneck claims remain hypotheses. The source performs sequential deterministic generation, randomized recursive Lomuto quicksort, a linear sortedness check and conditional MD5 over native int bytes. ARM64 with four CPU cores and no GPU favors complementary experiments in comparison sorting, integer radix sorting and exact generation. Correctness depends on reproducing the generated multiset and final sorted bytes, not the original pivot sequence. All approaches must remain general across valid inputs; no expected-answer substitution, test-value specialization or changes to the experimental configuration.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"ed04dde25e24829bf86b8f645b0137d52b5e1448a8614be5a7e47c7971bfd59c\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research a low-overhead comparison-sort replacement for the recursive randomized Lomuto quicksort. Start with deterministic median-of-three pivots, efficient two-sided partitioning, insertion sorting for small ranges, bounded recursion and a worst-case fallback; investigate duplicate-aware partitioning where useful. Removing pivot RNG calls is safe after generation and avoids races on the global RNG state. Compare the improved serial kernel with coarse-grained parallel sorting of disjoint partitions, using at most four workers and only threading facilities supported by the unchanged build. Tune general size/task cutoffs rather than specializing to benchmark inputs. Measure whole-program performance: at roughly 69 ms baseline runtime, task startup and synchronization could outweigh parallel gains.\",\"B\":\"Research integer radix sorting as an independent alternative to comparison sorting. Compare a simple buffered byte-wise LSD implementation against a wider-digit variant, balancing pass count, histogram footprint and memory traffic. Preserve signed int ordering: for 32-bit ints, sorting keys formed by XOR with the sign bit avoids assuming the generator always produces nonnegative values. Explore four-worker passes with private histograms, prefix-derived disjoint output ranges and stable scatter, without per-element atomics. Retain a serial path for small arrays. Use checked allocation sizes and a correct low-memory fallback. Ensure MD5 receives the actual final sorted buffer without an unnecessary final copy where possible. Select variants by end-to-end measurements, not pass count alone.\",\"C\":\"Research exact case-generation and other non-sorting overhead reductions, producing changes independently composable with A or B. The two multiply-with-carry RNG streams have serial dependencies; investigate modest unrolling first, then exact modular skip-ahead for independent contiguous generation chunks if justified. Chunk initialization must reproduce the original sequence, never use independent seeds. Preserve the fixed reference's unsigned arithmetic, conversion behavior and generated int bytes. In particular, do not replace drand(0, INT_MAX) with a raw RNG integer without proving equivalence: floating-point multiplication, division and truncation can affect results. Treat abs/INT_MIN behavior as another compatibility hazard. Consider generation/histogram fusion only as a separately measured integration. Preserve sortedness validation and MD5's sequential chaining; never substitute independent chunk digests or cached answers.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only programs and improvements delivered by the research trees. Keep the best validated standalone candidate and the baseline available. Treat A and B primarily as competing sorting engines; test C with each promising engine separately before considering more complex hybrids. Reconcile RNG ownership, worker scheduling, scratch buffers and final-buffer ownership explicitly. Require unchanged correctness checks plus source-level reasoning about edge cases, allocation handling and exact generated bytes. Preserve input/error behavior, sortedness checking, conditional MD5 computation and output formatting. Use the existing measurement protocol and fixed compiler, target and budgets. Compare complete programs, including generation, allocation and hashing; reject regressions and do not assume gains combine additively.\",\"analysis\":\"This run targets Problem B in src/quicksort.c, not the other supplied problems. The valid baseline averaged 0.06909 seconds over three tightly clustered samples and passed four correctness cases. No input sizes or phase timings are supplied, so bottleneck claims remain hypotheses. The source performs sequential deterministic generation, randomized recursive Lomuto quicksort, a linear sortedness check and conditional MD5 over native int bytes. ARM64 with four CPU cores and no GPU favors complementary experiments in comparison sorting, integer radix sorting and exact generation. Correctness depends on reproducing the generated multiset and final sorted bytes, not the original pivot sequence. All approaches must remain general across valid inputs; no expected-answer substitution, test-value specialization or changes to the experimental configuration.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"nonce\":\"5f4470e79f8c40d28a28e12c00c025ee\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"xhigh\",\"request_sha256\":\"ed04dde25e24829bf86b8f645b0137d52b5e1448a8614be5a7e47c7971bfd59c\",\"session_id\":\"2bd8b683b45b41c8b48ec38708f46bab\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"4def2b20b0ba623fd7924091bf27046a18fd5caa00e84ba88dfa387cb21b9c06\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":12447,\"output_tokens\":3220,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":2454}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"xhigh\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":15667,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
